# Knowledge

A personal knowledge base built from curiosity — every note here started as a simple, sometimes "silly," question and was pushed deeper through self-directed inquiry until it became real understanding.

## Purpose

This folder is not a collection of textbook summaries. It is a record of **how I actually learn**: asking questions, chasing the answers, questioning those answers, and going deeper until a topic makes sense in my own words. Each file captures both the *knowledge* and the *thought process* that led to it, so revisiting a topic means re-experiencing how I understood it — not just re-reading facts.

## Why This Exists

- To turn scattered curiosity into a searchable, structured archive.
- To make relearning fast: instead of starting from zero, I can reread how I already broke a topic down.
- To track how my understanding evolves over time — from a basic question to a deep, connected grasp of a subject.
- To use as a reference base for AI-assisted learning: when I want to go deep on any topic, this knowledge can be fed in so explanations build on what I already know instead of starting over.

## Guiding Principle

> Understanding isn't given — it's built, one question at a time.

This archive grows continuously. It is incomplete by design, and that's fine: it holds what I know *today*, and it updates as I learn more *tomorrow*.

## Usage Notes

- New knowledge is added regularly — treat this as a living document, not a finished one.
- When using this with an AI assistant, share relevant topic files so explanations can build on existing understanding rather than repeating the basics.
- Prioritize clarity over polish — the goal is genuine understanding, not perfect prose.
